We have derived improved differentiability properties for solutions to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
  \begin{equation*}
  \min \left\{\int_{\Omega}f\left(x, Dv(x)\right)dx\,:\, v\in
  \mathcal{K}_{\psi}\left(\Omega\right)\right\},
  \end{equation*}
  where the function $f$ is strictly convex and satisfies a $p$-growth condition with respect to the gradient variable. With regard to regularity, we have obtained results when $f$ is of $(2,q)$-type. This improvement in regularity holds for domains and obstacles that are $s$-H\"older continuous, where $s=1$ when the growth exponent $\p$ lies in the range $(1,p)$, and $s=p$ when $\p$ is greater than or equal to $q$. This research builds upon and extends the findings in the work of Krist\'a\'nik and Str\'a\'snov\'a.
